      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- React official docs — react.dev (Learn + Reference, especially \"Thinking in React\" and the Server Components guidance).\n- Next.js official docs — nextjs.org/docs (App Router, Rendering, and Data Fetching sections).\n- web.dev — Core Web Vitals and performance guidance maintained by the Chrome team.\n- roadmap.sh/frontend — community-maintained frontend developer roadmap.\n- \"Refactoring UI\" by Adam Wathan & Steve Schoger — practical, developer-focused UI design decisions.\n- Kent C. Dodds — Testing JavaScript / Epic React (testing-library philosophy: \"test behavior, not implementation\").\n- Josh W. Comeau's blog (joshwcomeau.com) — deep, visual explanations of CSS, React rendering, and animation.\n- Patterns.dev — modern rendering patterns (SSR/SSG/ISR/streaming) and React design patterns.\n- MDN Web Docs — canonical reference for HTML, CSS, ARIA, and Web APIs.\n- WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG) — w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg — canonical accessibility patterns (combobox, dialog, listbox, etc.).",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- React official docs — react.dev (Learn + Reference, especially \"Thinking in React\" and the Server Components guidance).\n- Next.js official docs — nextjs.org/docs (App Router, Rendering, and Data Fetching sections).\n- web.dev — Core Web Vitals and performance guidance maintained by the Chrome team.\n- roadmap.sh/frontend — community-maintained frontend developer roadmap.\n- \"Refactoring UI\" by Adam Wathan & Steve Schoger — practical, developer-focused UI design decisions.\n- Kent C. Dodds — Testing JavaScript / Epic React (testing-library philosophy: \"test behavior, not implementation\").\n- Josh W. Comeau's blog (joshwcomeau.com) — deep, visual explanations of CSS, React rendering, and animation.\n- Patterns.dev — modern rendering patterns (SSR/SSG/ISR/streaming) and React design patterns.\n- MDN Web Docs — canonical reference for HTML, CSS, ARIA, and Web APIs.\n- WAI-ARIA Authoring Practices Guide (APG) — w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg — canonical accessibility patterns (combobox, dialog, listbox, etc.).",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
